  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Abusive; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a teacher pointing out a mistake on a chalkboard to a student, with overlaid text that reads 'see here's your mistake' and 'you added a fuck that i didnt give.' The tone is confrontational and uses vulgar language, which can be interpreted as abusive. The meme is likely intended to humorously depict a scenario where someone is being corrected harshly, possibly in an academic or professional setting. The use of profanity and the aggressive tone of the text suggest an intent to mock or belittle the student, fitting the definition of abusive content. There is no indication of targeting specific protected characteristics, but the overall intent is to demean or insult the individual being corrected, which aligns with abusive intent.",
